@startuml BlasaCarDomainClassDiagram
left to right direction
hide empty methods

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 65
skinparam ranksep 60
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11

title BlasaCar - Domain Class Diagram

class User <<entity>> {
  id : bigint
  first_name : string
  last_name : string
  email : string
  phone : string
  password_hash : string
  profile_photo : string?
  email_verified : boolean
  phone_verified : boolean
  role : UserRole
  account_status : AccountStatus
  suspended_at : datetime?
}

class DriverProfile <<entity>> {
  id : bigint
  cin_number : string
  cin_front_photo : string?
  cin_back_photo : string?
  cin_verified : boolean
  /avg_rating : decimal(3,2)
  /total_trips : int
}

class Vehicle <<entity>> {
  id : bigint
  brand : string
  model : string
  photo : string?
}

class City <<entity>> {
  id : bigint
  name : string
}

class Ride <<entity>> {
  id : bigint
  departure_time : datetime
  price_per_seat : decimal(10,2)
  total_seats : int
  /available_seats : int
  meeting_point : string
  notes : text?
  admin_note : text?
  status : RideStatus
}

class Booking <<entity>> {
  id : bigint
  seats_reserved : int
  status : BookingStatus
  booked_at : datetime
}

class Review <<entity>> {
  id : bigint
  rating : tinyint
  comment : text?
}

class Notification <<entity>> {
  id : bigint
  type : string
  channel : NotificationChannel
  title : string
  message : text
  recipient_phone : string?
  delivery_status : NotificationDeliveryStatus?
  provider : string?
  provider_message_id : string?
  sent_at : datetime?
  failed_at : datetime?
  delivery_error : text?
  is_read : boolean
}

enum UserRole {
  admin
  driver
  traveler
}

enum AccountStatus {
  active
  suspended
}

enum RideStatus {
  scheduled
  completed
  cancelled
}

enum BookingStatus {
  pending
  confirmed
  rejected
  cancelled
  completed
}

enum NotificationChannel {
  in_app
  whatsapp
}

enum NotificationDeliveryStatus {
  pending
  sent
  failed
}

' Core domain relationships
User "1" -- "0..1" DriverProfile : has
DriverProfile "1" -- "1..*" Vehicle : owns
Vehicle "1" -- "0..*" Ride : used for
City "1" <-- "0..*" Ride : departure
City "1" <-- "0..*" Ride : arrival
User "1" -- "0..*" Booking : traveler
Ride "1" -- "0..*" Booking : has
Booking "1" -- "0..1" Review : receives
User "1" -- "0..*" Notification : receives
Ride "0..1" <-- "0..*" Notification : ride context
Booking "0..1" <-- "0..*" Notification : booking context

' Enum type dependencies keep enum boxes connected in the rendered diagram.
User ..> UserRole : role
User ..> AccountStatus : account_status
Ride ..> RideStatus : status
Booking ..> BookingStatus : status
Notification ..> NotificationChannel : channel
Notification ..> NotificationDeliveryStatus : delivery_status

note right of Ride
Normalization:
Ride does not store a driver reference.

Functional dependency:
Vehicle -> DriverProfile
Ride -> Vehicle
therefore Ride -> DriverProfile transitively.

Business rules:
departure city must be different from arrival city.
/available_seats is derived from total_seats minus active bookings.
end note

note bottom of Vehicle
Business rule:
the vehicle used for a ride must belong to
the driver publishing that ride.
end note

note bottom of Booking
Business rules:
seats_reserved must be at least 1.
A traveler cannot have duplicate active bookings
for the same ride.

Active statuses:
pending, confirmed.

Contact is visible only after the booking is
confirmed or completed.
end note

note right of Review
Normalization:
Review does not store traveler or driver.

Functional dependency:
Review -> Booking
Booking -> Traveler
Booking -> Ride
Ride -> Vehicle
Vehicle -> DriverProfile

Business rules:
one review per booking.
rating must be between 1 and 5.
end note

note bottom of DriverProfile
/avg_rating is derived from received review ratings.
/total_trips is derived from completed rides.

CIN validation requires front and back photos.
end note

note bottom of Notification
recipient_phone is a delivery snapshot.
It is kept to preserve the exact phone used
when the notification was sent.
end note

@enduml
